Z||000000||Oreif||03-04-2000||09:08 PM||||Today I have finished the entire front suspension. It includes: All poly bushings, 1 1/4" sway bar, New ball joints, Tie rods, bearings, cross-drilled rotors, Brake pads, calipers, steel braided brake lines, lower springs (1",) KYB shocks, and Powder coated A-arms and brake shield.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Tomorrow I get to tear the entire back apart!<BR>Question has anyone installed the aftermarket rear sway bar and do you use the front hole or the rear hole on the A-arm? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-04-2000||09:20 PM||||Oreif, I need to do the same I keep putting it off. I want to lower F&R of my 86SE What springs are you using? What is the rate? How does the ride feel?. Also I want to do the bushings on the 87coupe but i'm thinking of stock rubber bushing on it. Can you post a pic, does 1" realy look any different? I have stock 14's and just want to close the gap a bit, 1"-2"??||||reg||1
