Z||000003||Oreif||03-05-2000||01:03 AM||||I am using the springs that came with the Fiero Store KYB set-up. Right now I have a cheap set of 13" steel wheels (I use for storing car during winter) But the wheel/tire fills the wheel well very nice! As for ride I have not driven it. A friend had the same thing done to his 87 GT and I test drove it with the same set-up I'm using. The ride was stiff but not excessive. I have driven a car that had the KONI race suspension and it was too stiff for street driving. It felt like the shocks were just a steel bars. As soon as I finish the rear I plane on taking pics of the suspension and I am also going to park the car the same way I have in one picture and post them side by side so everyone can see the difference.<P>Batboy ~ Thanks for the link on the rear swaybar how to. ||||reg||1
